WEBVTT

NOTE
AI-generated narration. Synthetic demonstration data.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:11.867
Meet FinPulse, Alloyce Amos's credit data engineering project. This interactive demo follows synthetic events from their raw source to validated records and useful data products.

2
00:00:12.187 --> 00:00:21.670
The overview connects five markets in one operating picture. Counts and quality measures come from the same event pipeline, and each currency keeps its own totals.

3
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:31.712
Open the event explorer to inspect the original envelope and the related customer events. The source remains visible, so an unexpected metric can be traced back to evidence.

4
00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:42.063
Choose the invalid scenario and simulate a new batch. These records enter the raw bronze layer first. The original input stays available before any validation or correction.

5
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:54.719
In the pipeline studio, run the Python validation rules, dimensional loader, and SQL marts. Inspect the processing trace as raw events become validated silver records and gold aggregates.

6
00:00:55.039 --> 00:01:06.259
The quality lab explains each exception. Duplicates are suppressed, while late events can pass with a warning. Invalid records stay in quarantine until a reviewed correction is ready.

7
00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:17.210
Review a proposed correction and approve its replay. The original raw event is preserved, and the corrected result follows the pipeline again. This makes remediation traceable.

8
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:29.681
Market insights show counts, ratios, and values by country. Kenyan shillings, Ugandan shillings, Ghanaian cedis, Tanzanian shillings, and Zambian kwacha are kept separate.

9
00:01:30.001 --> 00:01:40.522
The data product catalogue connects outputs to their lineage. Follow a product through the processing stages, inspect its schema, or export its records for further analysis.

10
00:01:40.842 --> 00:01:52.219
FinPulse demonstrates validation, quality controls, replay, and reporting on synthetic credit data. Explore the working demo and source code; no new real credit decision is made here.
